# Day-23: Rust crate build artifacts for the Naga SPIR-V→WGSL
# transpiler. Source (Cargo.toml, src/, .cargo/) is tracked; the
# ~4 MB compiled target/ is regenerated by the documented Rust build step.
# Cargo.lock is tracked because Naga and its transitive graph are build inputs.
tools/naga-spirv-wgsl/target/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Game-derived artifacts. NEVER commit or publish these.
#
# The prebuilt JIT cache contains compiled translations of the
# game's own PowerPC code, and save states contain game memory
# images. Both are derivative works of a copyrighted commercial
# title. They are build/runtime conveniences, regenerable locally,
# and must not appear in a public repository.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
cores/dolphin/prebuilt-jit-cache.bin
*.gci
*.raw
*.iso
*.gcm
*.ciso
*.rvz

# Local research/scratch trees and harness output. Not part of the
# distributable project.
logs/
scratch-backlog/
uber-test/
.claude/
*.patch
!patches/**/*.patch

# The patched upstream tree is generated by fetch:dolphin + patch:upstream
# from the pinned commit and the locked patch series. It is reproducible
# output, not source, and committing it as a gitlink breaks the provenance
# flow that expects to manage the checkout itself.
vendor/dolphin/

# Release artifacts (GPL corresponding-source archives are built, not tracked)
dist/

# Pinned macOS/Linux core toolchain (tools/toolchain/bootstrap.sh)
.tools/
# A worktree may link vendor/ to a shared checkout (docs/repro-build.md)
/vendor
# Crates vendored for the GPL source archive (tools/build-corresponding-source.mjs)
tools/naga-spirv-wgsl/vendor/
